{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "label": "File log sink", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_filesink", "label": "FileSink", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Writes records to files named after the moment they were opened; queues on write and drains on a timer, on a full batch, and on shutdown."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_filesinkoptions", "label": "FileSinkOptions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_rotation", "label": "File rotation triggers", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Size and clock triggers combine, and rotateInterval means the clock boundary rather than 24 hours after startup - a process started at 09:41 rolls at the next midnight. A name collision gets a numeric suffix instead of appending to somebody else file."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_open_next_stamped_file", "label": "Rolling opens a new file, never renames", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Windows refuses to rename an open file, so a rename-based scheme either fails there or has to close the file first and race whatever is still writing. Opening the next stamped file has neither problem, and it means every file on disk is complete under the name it was always going to have - the same answer pino-roll and winston-daily-rotate-file arrived at."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_no_split_records", "label": "No record split across two files", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The rotation check runs before each line rather than per batch, so a batch that crosses the size limit finishes the current line, rolls, and continues in the new file."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_retention", "label": "File retention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Retention only ever deletes this sink own files: a candidate must match the configured prefix, the configured extension and the exact timestamp shape, and the active file is never a candidate - so a log directory shared with a sibling service survives intact. That is also why prefix exists. Compression runs after the new file is open, so a slow gzip never stalls records waiting behind it."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_durability", "label": "File sink durability window", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Batching leaves a window up to flush-interval in which a record has been logged but not written, which is the trade every high-throughput logger makes against a syscall per record. What is not at risk is the file itself: writes loop until every byte is accepted, rotation never renames, and terminate drains the queue - so a crashed process leaves a file complete up to some record boundary, never a corrupt one."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_sink_disable_on_permanent_failure", "label": "Disable the sink on permanent failure", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A directory that cannot be created or written - a read-only mount, a wrong path - disables the sink after one console message rather than failing every flush forever: the condition is permanent by nature, the application is otherwise fine, and a message every two seconds for the life of the process helps nobody."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_sink_cross_runtime", "label": "One file-sink implementation for Bun, Node and Deno", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The append handle, readdir and unlink all come from node:fs/promises, which Bun and Deno compatibility layers cover, so there is no per-runtime adapter - and a smoke case runs the sink on all three to keep the claim honest."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_prefix_extension_safety", "label": "Prefix and extension may not contain a dot or separator", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "They are built into both the filename and the pattern retention matches on, and a stray parent-directory segment would point deletions somewhere nobody meant."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_filesink", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_filesinkoptions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_rotation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_open_next_stamped_file", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_no_split_records", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_retention", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_durability", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_sink_disable_on_permanent_failure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_sink_cross_runtime", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_file_log_sink", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_prefix_extension_safety", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/observability/logging/file-sink.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_open_next_stamped_file", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_observability_logging_file_sink_rotation", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED",